descriptionByLocale.en:
Integrated with the Infrastructure department and under the responsibility of the Chief Technical Team, your main mission will be to create and manage detailed digital models throughout the building's life cycle (design, construction, operation). In this context, your main responsibilities will be:

• Manage revisions and updates to 2D plans and BIM models throughout the building life cycle;

• Participate in updating building data (plans, BIM model) in the operational phase;

• Produce digital models in accordance with BIM requirements throughout the building life cycle;

• Participate and perform Scan to BIM;

• Conduct collision analyses and simulations to detect potential conflicts and propose solutions;

• Create the catalogue of BIM objects and participate in updating the internal BIM templates;

• Participate in the development of BIM procedures, in particular the management of plan update requests and the systematic storage of data and files;

• Work with internal and external stakeholders to meet BIM requirements;

• Assist in the selection and implementation of BIM software and technologies;

• Assist in selecting innovative BIM tools;

• Develop, manage and edit documents and drawings for presentations at sessions;

• Be able to interpret a COC or BIM charter;

• Integrate HSE requirements (risk areas, clearances);

• Take into account local regulations (safety at work, accessibility, evacuation, traffic, free height), OCIRT standards, SUVA standards, depending on canton/site;

• Ensure the reliability, updating and accessibility of data within the operating tool (GMAO);

• To manage the life cycle of assets and their evolution, including maintenance contracts, technical attributes, work release data, as well as updating digital models and associated graphic documentation.

• You have advanced training in building engineering, architecture, construction or an equivalent field.

• You ideally have BIM certification or proven experience in this field.

• You show a strong interest in innovation, digitalisation and the evolution of working methods in the construction sector.

• You master BIM tools and have a good understanding of building management and operation processes.

• You can effectively manage priorities and coordinate multiple missions simultaneously in a dynamic environment.

• You have a solid understanding of the different phases of a work's life cycle, from design to operation, to construction.

• You have an analytical mindset, autonomy, rigour and a real ability to collaborate with multidisciplinary teams.

• You benefit from a particular experience or sensitivity to industrial environments and their operational and regulatory constraints, which is a real asset.

What we offer:
• Insurance coverage - disease (basic and supplementary)
• 5 annual weeks of leave with 2 additional weeks between Christmas and New Year thanks to the daily accumulation of additional minutes
• Contributions to your sports or cultural activities as well as subscriptions encouraging soft mobility (e.g. SBB)
• An LPP with favourable rates
Would you like to express your expertise at Audemars Piguet? Don't hesitate and apply online! We look forward to discussing the opportunities that might match your next professional adventure.
